r bomber that carried 10,000 lbs of bombs, more than a B-24\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eJohn McCain and Paul Galante (POW for 7 years) both flew this type\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAir Force F-4s also used tail hooks on wet Vietnam runways; approach speed 250 mph, up to 58,000 lbs\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLake Michigan carrier training in WWII\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTwo converted coal-fired paddle steamers used as training carriers (pilots based at Glenview, IL and Michigan)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e~18,000 pilots trained; ~100-130 aircraft sank, recovered in the mid-1990s\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGeorge H.W. Bush completed carrier quals on USS Sable in August 1943, age 18\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSBD Dauntless on display: recovered from 240 ft, flipped on takeoff and run over by the ship, not restorable\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003eEjection Seats, Medals, and Tuskegee Airmen\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEjection seat evolution: WWII pilots had to manually bail out; Germans invented seats for jets (500+ mph)\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eF-101 Voodoo used a mortar shell to blow the canopy and punch the pilot out\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eModern “zero-zero” seats: computer-controlled, multi-motor, work from dead stop on runway\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFactors in attitude, altitude, and oxygen; deploys drogue chute at high altitude, main chute at 15,000 ft\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTrade-off: severe spinal compression; a museum staffer who ejected twice from an F-14 over the Indian Ocean is a regular VA patient\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMedal of Honor: most awarded in the Civil War (only medal given then); Dr. Mary Walker the sole female recipient, formally reinstated by Congress in 1977\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTuskegee Airmen: never lost a bomber to the Luftwaffe on any escorted mission\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHarry Stewart Jr. shot down three ME-262 jets (100+ mph faster than his P-51D) through superior maneuvering\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWon the 1949 Air Force Top Gun competition at Nellis; Truman desegregated the military in 1947\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRecommended film: \u003cem\u003eDouble Victory\u003c/em\u003e (YouTube); \u003cem\u003eRed Tails\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003eThe Tuskegee Airmen\u003c/em\u003e described as Hollywoodized\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"12:[\"$\",\"$L23\",null,{\"resourceId\":\"c274ba56-ccf0-4bbe-96bd-ccee8858102a\",\"resourceType\":\"document\",\"creatorName\":\"Chris Sorensen\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L24\",null,{\"joinName\":\"Chris Sorensen\",\"type\":\"meeting\",\"variant\":\"modal\",\"creatorInfo\":{\"name\":\"Chris Sorensen\",\"avatar\":\"https://d2y2qtsuzmwn83.cloudfront.net/f9164abfa6b7baae860a51927564c7d6?v=3\",\"workspaceName\":null}}],[\"$\",\"main\",null,{\"className\":\"relative flex w-screen flex-col overflow-hidden bg-white supports-[height:100cqh]:h-[100cqh] supports-[height:100svh]:h-[100svh]\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L25\",null,{\"documentId\":\"c274ba56-ccf0-4bbe-96bd-ccee8858102a\",\"documentPanel\":{\"document\":{\"id\":\"c274ba56-ccf0-4bbe-96bd-ccee8858102a\",\"title\":\"Fighter jet technology insights\",\"created_at\":\"2026-07-23T17:20:51.080Z\",\"ydoc_version\":2,\"owner\":{\"id\":\"870a61ad-2e3b-4cb7-b9ce-fe467e7e57f7\",\"name\":\"Chris Sorensen\",\"picture\":\"https://d2y2qtsuzmwn83.cloudfront.net/f9164abfa6b7baae860a51927564c7d6?v=3\"}},\"panel\":{\"id\":\"889999bf-99e1-434e-91d0-288d5b757b35\",\"document_id\":\"c274ba56-ccf0-4bbe-96bd-ccee8858102a\",\"title\":\"Summary\",\"content\":{\"type\":\"doc\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"heading\",\"attrs\":{\"id\":null,\"level\":3},\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Phantom II and Early Jet F